From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Martin=20=C5=A0trobl?= <recordyletsplays@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:47:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] ANDROID: arm64: dts: exynos7870: Add the normal reboot
 mode

S-Boot keeps booting what INFORM3 says: after a boot into recovery, a
plain reboot went to recovery again, because nothing rewrote the
register. The vendor kernel writes 0x12345670 ("unknown reason") there on
every reboot without a mode of its own (sec_reboot.c). Add it as
mode-normal.

To be replaced by the same change in the mainline series.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi
index beb959c39a52..a0c51996009d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi
@@ -500,6 +500,7 @@ reboot-mode {
 				offset = <0x080c>;
 				mode-bootloader = <0x1234567d>;
 				mode-download = <0x12345671>;
+				mode-normal = <0x12345670>;
 				mode-recovery = <0x12345674>;
 			};
 		};
